# Protections for the SROP-no-writable-segment variant corpus. Held IDENTICAL
# across every target in this family on purpose: the *ELF shape* (which PT_LOAD
# segments exist, where the symbol table lands, the count-returning wrapper, and
# the bare syscall) is the only variable, so a protection difference would
# confound the measurement.
#
# The category REQUIRES a static image with NO writable PT_LOAD, so the ordinary
# SROP path (stage a frame in .data, or point rsp at a leaked stack) is
# unavailable and the only controllable [rsp] for the post-sigreturn
# `syscall; ret` is a qword in the symbol table, mapped past p_filesz in the
# tail page of an R / R E segment.
#
# -nostdlib   no libc: no CRT _start, no .init/.fini, no GOT/PLT, and -- the
#             point -- no writable data pulled in by the C runtime. The whole
#             program is the hand-written _start/read/write/vuln asm below.
# -static     no dynamic loader, no PT_INTERP, no .dynamic (a .dynamic would be a
#             writable segment). A truly self-contained image.
# -no-pie     fixed load address (0x400000): the symbol-table st_value fields the
#             pivot reads sit at known absolute vaddrs, which is what lets the
#             technique work with no leak at all.
#
# NB: build_all.sh prepends COMMON_FLAGS (incl. -g); its debug sections are
# non-alloc and do not perturb the two-PT_LOAD / symtab-in-mapped-tail layout.
-nostdlib
-static
-no-pie
